## Interface: 120100
## Title: KeyMode
## Notes: Switches to a lean set of addons for Mythic+ and raids, and back to your full setup afterwards, with one command and one reload
## Author: Tharavol, Claude
## Version: @project-version@
## IconTexture: Interface\Icons\INV_Relics_Hourglass
## X-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
## X-Website: https://github.com/Tharavol/KeyMode
## X-ReleaseNotes: Switches a character to a lean set of addons for Mythic+ dungeons and raids, and back to its full setup afterwards, with one reload. Two account-wide lists name what to turn off: the Instance list in keystone dungeons and raids, the optional World list the rest of the time. The first switch records the character's exact enable state, and Off restores precisely that. Turning an addon off also turns off everything that requires it, and turning one back on brings its required dependencies, so a switch never leaves a missing-dependency error. Every switch first shows a preview of what will be turned off and on and reloads only on Confirm. KeyMode offers Instance mode on entering a raid or a Mythic dungeon in a group, or on joining or listing a Mythic+ or raid group, and World mode afterwards; prompts never appear in combat or during an active key, "Not now" silences one until the next reload, and each can be turned off. Lists are edited under Options > AddOns > KeyMode > Lists, with suggested lists worked out from what is installed, and can be exported and imported as text. Protected addons are never turned off. Switch with /km instance, /km world and /km off (alias /keymode), the minimap button, the Addon Compartment entry or a key binding; /km help lists every command. Source, issues and release notes: https://github.com/Tharavol/KeyMode
